      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain the difference between high glycemic index and low glycemic index foods? specifically why it matters for insulin.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index (GI) foods cause rapid spikes in blood sugar, forcing the pancreas to secrete large amounts of insulin quickly, whereas low GI foods release sugar slowly and result in a gentle, manageable insulin response. This matters because frequent high insulin surges can lead to insulin resistance over time, making it harder for your body to manage blood glucose effectively. Additionally, low GI foods tend to improve satiety and support healthier weight maintenance compared to the erratic hunger cycles often triggered by high GI foods.",
